data/outputs/**
# The measured-spectrum Parquet store. It is INPUT data, not a generated output, so it sits
# beside data/processed rather than under data/outputs -- which means the rule above no longer
# covers it and it needs its own entry. It must stay out of git regardless of size: it is
# derived from the NIST WebBook and is not redistributable.
data/nist_spectra/
*.pyc
**/__pycache__/
mol-spectro.sif
.secrets/
.pytest_cache/

# Copyrighted reference material: the McLafferty textbook PDF plus scans of its
# endpaper/figures, kept locally as the provenance for the rules in
# src/data_generation/rules/IMS_*.py. Not redistributable, so not committed.
data/IMS-Book/

# (Derivation-graph dumps of every kind are ignored -- see data/processed*/ below.)

# The thesis tree is now merged into this repo under thesis/ (was a separate nested
# repo, gitignored while it lived here). It carries its own thesis/.gitignore, which
# git applies normally now that this directory is no longer excluded -- that nested
# file is what keeps LaTeX build artifacts and the copyrighted thesis/report/literature/
# PDFs out of the index. Do not re-add a "thesis/" line here: git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so it would silently disable the nested rules along with it.
#
# (The pre-publication embargo on pushing thesis/ to the public origin was lifted in
# 2026-08; the branch is pushed and tracks normally.)
_minted-main/**
_minted/
_minted-*/

# Per-agent staging area for in-progress mechanism records (validated, then promoted)
data/mechanisms/.staging/

# ALL derivation-graph dumps: the corpus of record in data/processed/ and the side-by-side
# A/B rebuild targets (PROCESSED_DIR_OVERRIDE=...) beside it. data/processed/ used to be
# tracked; at 2070 files / 1.03 GB it was essentially the entire repository, and the working
# tree is now 45 GB. Dumps are reproducible from data/compounds.csv plus the rule library, so
# they are rebuilt, not cloned. Untracked in 2026-08 -- note the 1.03 GB of blobs remain in
# history and only a filter-repo rewrite would remove them.
data/processed*/
